    <!-- Camera placement, in one line: the rest is said live by the placement banner. A pushup is
         read across the shoulders from the head and along the torso from the side. A plank is
         read from the 3-D skeleton, so from the head and from the side both work, and the legs are
         taken from the skeleton whether the camera sees them or not: the hint does not ask for them.
         Its hint says the phone on its side, by the owner's decision: the screen turns with the phone
         for a plank, and side on the wide picture holds the body from 1.5-2 m where upright needed
         much more (PlankRigTest). -->
    <string name="exercise_hint_pushup">폰은 바닥에, 머리 앞쪽이나 옆으로 1m쯤 떨어뜨려 세워 두세요</string>
